<description>
Recolor every unobstructed background row or column spanning between opposite colored border cells green.

Input structure
- The grid has a black background with red and teal foreground cells on the borders and as blockers.
- Some full rows or columns have foreground cells at both opposite edges and only background cells between them.

Rule
- For each row, if the leftmost and rightmost cells are foreground and every interior cell is background, recolor that interior row green.
- For each column, if the top and bottom cells are foreground and every interior cell is background, recolor that interior column green.
- Preserve all original foreground cells and all blocked rows or columns.

Key insight
- The green cells mark edge-to-edge clear corridors, not enclosed areas; any original foreground cell inside the span blocks that row or column.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "black cells in full rows or columns whose opposite edge cells are foreground and whose interior span has no foreground blocker",
  "transform": "recolor those unobstructed interior row/column cells to green; preserve original foreground cells and all blocked spans"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-14 rows x 10-14 cols, square
  background: black
  colors: red (2) and teal (8) foreground; green (3) reserved for output
  border:
    every border cell is foreground (red or teal)
    border loop has exactly 2 color transitions, splitting it into two contiguous arcs
    partition style varies -- horizontal, vertical, or L-shaped (3 corners same, 1 differs)
  interior_blockers:
    each color forms exactly one 4-connected component across the full grid (border + interior)
    interior foreground density 18-27% of (H-2)x(W-2) cells
    blockers are placed to block some row/column corridors while leaving others clear
  corridors:
    row corridor = row where both border endpoints are foreground and all interior cells are black
    column corridor = column where both border endpoints are foreground and all interior cells are black
    unblocked row corridors: 1-6 [observed >= 2]
    unblocked column corridors: 1-3 [observed >= 1]
    at least 1 of each kind required (solver asserts)
    corridors need not be contiguous
  transform:
    fill interior cells of each unblocked row corridor with green
    fill interior cells of each unblocked column corridor with green
    intersections get green; original foreground cells unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N x N in [10, 14].
    2. Choose a border partition -- pick 2 transition points on the border loop to divide it into a red arc and a teal arc (each arc >= N cells). Fill all border cells accordingly.
    3. Choose 1-4 corridor rows (not row 0 or N-1) and 1-3 corridor columns (not col 0 or N-1). Leave their interior cells black.
    4. For non-corridor rows/columns, place interior foreground blockers so that every non-corridor row with two foreground border endpoints has at least one blocker in its interior span (and likewise for columns). Use a mix of red and teal.
    5. Ensure each color (red, teal) forms a single connected component across the whole grid. Grow blockers from same-color border regions inward via flood-fill or random walk. Retry or adjust if connectivity breaks.
    6. Verify interior foreground density is 15-30%.
    7. Input = the grid with corridors left black. Output = fill corridor interiors with green.
```
</generation_spec>
